    "result_text": "The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test-bearing class in the project (the other two files under `acceptance/` are the base class and audit support), so this is the complete suite.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `title` \u2192 `salutation` feature end-to-end:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `title` property to the `OwnerFields` request schema (so `OwnerFieldsDto` carries it) and a `readOnly` `salutation` property to the `Owner` response schema (so `OwnerDto` exposes it).\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `title` field with `@Column(name = \"title\")` plus getter/setter, so the value survives the create\u2192persist\u2192GET round-trip.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `title` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb \u2014 used by tests \u2014 plus h2, mysql, postgres for consistency).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added a `salutation` MapStruct expression: `title + \" \" + lastName` when a title is present, otherwise just `lastName`.\n\nThe existing POST pipeline (`ValidateOwnerRequiredFields` \u2192 `BuildOwner` via `ownerMapper.toOwner`) carries `title` through automatically since MapStruct maps the matching property, and the GET responder recomputes `salutation` from the loaded entity. The new `coreComposesSalutation` test passes and the full suite builds green.",
